// Container file systems (docs/filesystems.md): open an archive, a
// compressed file, a file system image or a firmware package as a tree of
// files, nested to any depth (a squashfs in a tar.gz in a zip), browse it,
// read and describe its files, import the programs in it (one, many, or a
// whole tree: batch import) and extract files to the daemon's host. Added
// in api_minor 48 (feature "filesystems").
//
// A session is the outermost container and what is mounted inside it; it
// belongs to the identity that opened it (anyone else, admins excepted,
// gets NOT_FOUND) and closes after 30 minutes unused. Paths name a file
// through every layer: '!' separates the layers and each layer is a path
// of percent-encoded components ("/rootfs.sqfs!/bin/busybox"); use the
// paths a listing returns. Names from a container are display text only:
// nothing is written to the host except by ExtractFromFileSystem, which
// sanitizes them. Every container is untrusted input, read within limits
// (FileSystemLimits).

